<title>UK: Reed Intl proposes share split.</title>
<headline>Reed Intl proposes share split.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reed International said on Wednesday a proposal would be put to its AGM next month that the company undertake a two-for-one split of its ordinary shares.</p>
<p>The record date for the subdivision would be the close of business on May 2, with the first dealings in the subdivided shares taking place on May 6.</p>
<p>If the resolution is approved one Elsevier ordinary share will be the economic equivalent to 1.538 of a split Reed ordinary share. Currently one Elsevier ordinary share is equivalent to 0.769 of a Reed share.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
